    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Keene-State-College/Adjunct-Faculty---Chemistry_JR10332": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Department of Chemistry at Keene State College is seeking qualified applicants for an adjunct faculty position for the Spring 2027 semester. Primary responsibilities will be to teach a one-semester laboratory-based course in analytical chemistry (CHEM 355) focusing on experimental techniques and instrumental methods of analysis. Other responsibilities will be to prepare and maintain teaching laboratory spaces and participate in department and/or unit meetings. The qualified candidate will have an advanced degree in chemistry with background and experience in analytical chemistry and/or chemical measurement. Duties/Responsibilities: (75% ) Delivery of an existing curriculum and course content in analytical chemistry. Preparation of lesson plans and some supplementary course materials. Ensuring safe working conditions for and modeling safe working habits to students. Assessment of student learning. Assignment of grades. Referring of students to support services where necessary. When appropriate, provide supplemental instruction and mentorship to students. (20%) Prepare laboratory spaces for instruction with the support of a lab technician. Provide basic upkeep of laboratory spaces. Provide basic maintenance of laboratory equipment. Keep laboratory spaces clean and organized. (5%) Comply with USNH and KSC policies. Participate in department and/or unit meetings as appropriate. Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : Minimum qualifications for consideration are a Master’s degree in chemistry or a related discipline, a demonstrated background and experience in analytical chemistry, and a record of success in in-person teaching at the College/University level. For individuals pursuing a Doctoral degree, ABD candidates will be considered. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Demonstrated background and experience in analytical chemistry and/or chemical measurement . Ability to use basic analytical glassware to prepare, e.g., standard solutions and chemical reagents . Ability to perform basic analytical techniques, e.g., gravimetric analysis, manual titrations, sample preparation. Ability to analyze data using appropriate software tools. Ability to perform analysis using a wide range of chemical instrumentation, such as: Optical spectroscopy, Chromatography, Mass spectrometry, etc. Applicant Instructions Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/Cover Letter section of your application: Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration.  Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed.   Compensation Pay Range $800 Per Credit Hour (Masters in Science) or $840 Per Credit Hour (PhD) Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene Salary Grade: Period Activity"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Keene-State-College/Adjunct-Faculty---Chemistry_JR10333": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Department of Chemistry at Keene State College is seeking qualified applicants for an adjunct faculty position for the Spring 2027 semester. Primary responsibilities will be to teach General Chemistry [CHEM 111] lecture and its associated laboratory sections. All courses will be taught in person. This position supports the department by providing high-quality undergraduate teaching, evaluating student learning, and working collaboratively with full-time faculty. Duties/Responsibilities: (70%) Lecture Implementing a lecture curriculum to meet the course objectives. Syllabi and textbook will be provided. Using the college learning platform [Canvas] for grading and posting course materials. Designing graded assignment and exams for lecture. Assessment of student learning. Assignment of grades. Referring of students to support services where necessary. When appropriate, provide supplemental instruction and mentorship to students. (25%) Laboratory Delivery of an existing laboratory curriculum. Ensuring safe working conditions for and modeling safe laboratory working habits to students. Provide basic upkeep of laboratory spaces. Keep laboratory spaces clean and organized. (5%) Comply with USNH and KSC policies. Participate in department and/or unit meetings as appropriate. Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : Minimum qualifications for consideration are a Master’s degree in chemistry or a related discipline, and a record of success in in-person teaching at the College/University level. For individuals pursuing a Doctoral degree, ABD candidates will be considered. Applicant Instructions Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/Cover Letter section of your application: Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration.  Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed.   Compensation Pay Range $800 Per Credit Hour (Masters in Science) or $840 Per Credit Hour (PhD) Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene Salary Grade: Period Activity"
